# Test Timeout Enforcement

Always run `zig build test` with the `timeout` command set to less than 10 seconds to catch hanging tests early.

## Usage

```bash
# ❌ BAD - No timeout
zig build test

# ✅ GOOD - With timeout
timeout 10s zig build test
```

## Shell Tool

When using the Shell tool to run tests, wrap with `timeout`:

```
Shell(command: "timeout 10s zig build test", block_until_ms: 11000)
```

Note: Set `block_until_ms` slightly higher than the timeout value to allow the timeout command to terminate gracefully.

## Rationale

- Prevents tests from hanging indefinitely
- Provides fast feedback during development
- Catches deadlocks and infinite loops quickly
